.TH XG2G-ADMIN 8 "2026-07-30" "xg2g" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
xg2g-admin \- administer a persistent xg2g Linux installation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xg2g-admin
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xg2g-admin
is the supported lifecycle command for an xg2g installation managed by
systemd and Docker Compose.
It diagnoses the installed contract, creates and restores backups, applies
pinned updates with rollback protection, and removes installed runtime
artifacts.
.PP
Run host operations as root.
The command never partitions, formats, mounts, or deletes an external DVR
path.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Check prerequisites, permissions, storage, container health, and HTTPS.
.TP
.B backup
Create an atomic backup of durable SQLite and JSON state plus configuration.
.TP
.BI restore " ARCHIVE " \-\-yes
Validate and restore a backup after first creating a safety backup.
.TP
.BI update " \-\-ref TAG_OR_SHA"
Back up the current installation, install the pinned ref, health-check it, and
roll back automatically on failure.
.TP
.B rollback \-\-yes
Reinstall the ref recorded immediately before the last update.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove services and deployed runtime files while preserving configuration,
data, local backups, recordings, and external DVR storage.
.TP
.B uninstall \-\-purge-data \-\-yes
Also remove xg2g-managed configuration, state, Caddy state, and local backups.
External recordings and DVR storage remain untouched.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-install-root " DIR"
Prefix installed paths with
.IR DIR .
This option exists for packaging and lifecycle contract tests, not routine host
administration.
.TP
.B \-h
.TQ
.B \-\-help
Show command usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xg2g/xg2g.env
Root-owned service environment and secrets.
.TP
.I /var/lib/xg2g
Persistent runtime state.
.TP
.I /var/backups/xg2g
Default local backup directory.
.TP
.I /var/lib/xg2g/admin/previous-ref
Ref recorded for a governed rollback.
.TP
.I /srv/xg2g
Installed Compose, lifecycle, and verification bundle.
.SH SECURITY
Backups contain service configuration and may contain credentials.
Keep them root-owned, do not publish them, and verify archive provenance before
restoring.
.PP
Both
.B restore
and destructive data removal require explicit
.BR \-\-yes .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xg2g (1),
.BR docker (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/ManuGH/xg2g
https://github.com/ManuGH/xg2g
.UE
